@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="feed__head">
    <h1 class="feed__title">Privacy</h1>
</div>

<div class="prose">
    <p>
        Heardit stores your account (username, email address, and a hash of your password) and everything
        you post: your ratings, your written reviews, the reviews you like, who you follow, your bio, your
        favorite tracks, and your listen-later queue. Reviews, follows, your bio and your favorites are
        visible to anyone else with an account. A review shows how many likes it has, but not who liked
        it, and your queue is only shown to you. Nothing is sold or shared with anyone.
    </p>
    <p>
        Track players are embedded from spotify.com. Loading a page with a player means your browser talks
        to Spotify directly, and Spotify sets its own cookies and sees your IP address under
        <a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">its own privacy policy</a>.
        Heardit itself runs no analytics, no ad scripts, and no third-party trackers.
    </p>
    <p>
        There is no password recovery — no email is ever sent from this site, so a forgotten password can
        only be reset by whoever runs the database. To have your account and everything attached to it
        deleted, ask the site owner.
    </p>
</div>
